Subject: [PATCH] let the plugin's DiceCost and DiceLoss win the mmdet registry

UniAD v1's install guide pins mmdet 2.14.0. The paddock env runs mmdet 2.28.2
(it installs beside mmcv-full 1.7.2, which builds for CUDA 12.8 and sm_120),
and mmdet 2.28.2 registers a DiceCost and a DiceLoss of its own, so importing
projects.mmdet3d_plugin fails before any model is built:

    KeyError: 'DiceCost is already registered in Match Cost'

`force=True` keeps the plugin's own classes under those names, which is what
the UniAD configs mean by `type='DiceCost'` and `type='DiceLoss'` (the
panoptic head's mask matcher and mask loss; neither has weights, and neither
runs at test time). UniAD 2.0 made the same change. Registration happens at import,
before any setting is read, so nothing outside the source can do it.

---
diff --git a/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/core/bbox/match_costs/match_cost.py b/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/core/bbox/match_costs/match_cost.py
index d73b7e0..04cb6d2 100755
--- a/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/core/bbox/match_costs/match_cost.py
+++ b/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/core/bbox/match_costs/match_cost.py
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ class BBox3DL1Cost(object):
         return bbox_cost * self.weight
 
 
-@MATCH_COST.register_module()
+@MATCH_COST.register_module(force=True)  # mmdet 2.28 registers its own DiceCost
 class DiceCost(object):
     """IoUCost.
 
diff --git a/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/losses/dice_loss.py b/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/losses/dice_loss.py
index 3cb635f..fa7b08a 100644
--- a/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/losses/dice_loss.py
+++ b/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/losses/dice_loss.py
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ def dice_loss(input, target,mask=None,eps=0.001):
     d = (2 * a) / (b + c)
     return 1 - d
 
-@LOSSES.register_module()
+@LOSSES.register_module(force=True)  # mmdet 2.28 registers its own DiceLoss
 class DiceLoss(nn.Module):
 
     def __init__(self, eps=1e-6, reduction='mean', loss_weight=1.0):
